he took office during a global pandemic  and made battling covid19  his top priority promising 100 million  vaccines would be  administered by april we met that goal  last week by day 58  42 days ahead of schedule now today i'm  setting the second goal  and that is we will by my 100th day in  office  have administered 200 million shots  in people's arms that goal was exceeded  this week now more than 230 million  vaccines have been given out  with more than half of all americans  receiving at least  one dose what we're seeing is a  president who continues to be  disciplined  continues to stay on message and also a  president who continues to  focus on the issues and i think that's  what many americans  like to hear from their politicians  biden promised to ease  economic pain from the pandemic as well  delivering on a campaign promise to get  direct payments to millions of people  who were out of work  it not only addresses the immediate  crisis we're in it's better for the  long-term  economic health of our nation and our  competitiveness  by the end of march millions of  americans had received at least fourteen  hundred dollars  or more to help pay expenses like rent  and food  in his first 100 days biden also kept  another campaign pledge  rejoining the paris agreement on climate  change  that limits greenhouse gas emissions his  predecessor donald trump had pulled the  u.s  out biden rejoined the u.s on day one  to voters of color biden also delivered  on addressing systemic racism  in policing after the conviction of  derek shovin the police officer who  murdered george floyd  biden's justice department announced a  federal investigation  into the minneapolis police department  where chauvin was employed  and while biden did follow through on  his pledge to raise the minimum wage to  15 dollars an hour for federal  contractors  his plan to push for a federal minimum  wage  for everyone has faltered  his next goal to fix america's  infrastructure and create jobs  could be one of his most ambitious tasks  the theme of this first 100 days  could be characterized by terms such as  bold  daring and adventurous  biden repeatedly promises to meet the  moment  building back better from the covid  crisis channeling  a spirit not seen since president  roosevelt's new deal in the 1930s  building schools roads and parks and  lifting millions of americans wages  and quality of life following the great  depression  in that spirit president biden has  already expanded  america's social safety net and he's  promising more  biden's betting that americans are  looking for solutions to problems  like race and income inequality that he  believes  only government can deliver kimberly  hellcat al jazeera  washington
 

